  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "The position $x$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $x(t)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t}{\\operatorname{cot}\u2061t}.$ Calculate the velocity at time $t.$\n\n$v(t)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The velocity is the derivative of the position function $x(t)$ with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t}{\\operatorname{cot}\u2061t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{cot}\u2061t\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t(-{csc}^{2}\u2061t))}{{cot}^{2}\u2061t} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}\u2061t+t\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t{csc}^{2}\u2061t}{t})}{{cot}^{2}\u2061t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}\u2061t+t\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t{csc}^{2}\u2061t}{t{cot}^{2}\u2061t}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
